  "minimal_runtime_plan": [
    {
      "area": "authoritative rate commit",
      "change": "One always-on transaction owns requested/applied rate and stream generation; distribute an immutable pending configuration and collect DSP/effect/analysis/serializer acknowledgements. Apply once at a complete-frame boundary while muted. Do not add another parameter authority or pack metadata into 18-bit MIDI events."
    },
    {
      "area": "DDS and five timbres",
      "change": "Preserve exact current 48k canonical MIDI/ratio/gain tables and existing canonical slot steps. Fuse a unity or160/147 rate factor with the existing per-frame pitch multiplier so held phases, note assignments, velocity and pressure remain. Use full precision/rounding and the existing normalized0.45Fs audible cutoff after effective pitch; do not permanently zero gains solely due to the temporary44.1k mode. Validate high-note/partial clipping and reverse switches."
    },
    {
      "area": "ADSR, glide and LFO",
      "change": "Keep envelope level/state and canonical48k steps; scale per-frame attack/decay/release, glide delta and gain/morph/scale slew by160/147 for44.1. Sustain level, pitch-bend ratio and shape geometry remain rate-independent. Preserve main and vector distinct current ADSR semantics. Keep LFO phase and select a runtime phase increment. Existing cached voice steps/profile-less state prevents a naive ROM-bank switch from updating held voices."
    },
    {
      "area": "effects",
      "change": "Select runtime echo/chorus/early-reflection/FDN lengths from versioned48/44 banks inside existing maximum-sized storage. Re-derive damping poles and LFO/slew timing; preserve physical echo time and feedback semantics, verify stability/T60. Reset history through a dedicated rate-history command while retaining musical voices/parameters; do not reuse globalPANIC."
    },
    {
      "area": "DDR history fencing",
      "change": "Extend the existing ordered flush and return-marker transaction to include/acknowledge the rate configuration or generation before changing ECHO_SAMPLES in both audio consumer and DMA prefetch calculation. Drain/cancel old outstanding reads; do not reinterpret old ring samples at the new rate. Existing65-bit FIFO markers have no general stream generation field."
    },
    {
      "area": "FFT and display",
      "change": "Hann/twiddle geometry can remain; abort incomplete2048-frame captures/FFT work and prevent old-generation publication. Bind output metadata/frequency labels and bin-to-column choice to actualFs; fixed853-bin upper edge becomes18.367822kHz at44.1. Existing v1 layout fixes48000 and needs explicit version/capability treatment."
    },
    {
      "area": "CNN recognition",
      "change": "Keep the model/CQT at22050. The lowest-change path keeps the existing44.1-to48 analyzer-only adapter before the fixed147/320 polyphase frontend, with a new-rate restart/generation fence and pending DDR response protection. It is nearest-sample repetition, so validate accuracy; do not use it as the finalaudio resampler. A direct44.1-to22.05 1/2 filtered frontend is a separate coefficient/reproducibility/recognition-validation change."
    },
    {
      "area": "TF and cue time",
      "change": "TF NCO RATE_MUL=916260 is tied to76.8MHz; recompute when that clock changes and define mismatch SRC/controlled-switch policy. Keep48k control-cue timestamps as a canonical timebase and advance by48000/currentFs, or version timestamp units; do not silently stretch sequences. Closed recordings retain their own sample rate."
    }
